      m_Calls: []
  m_text: 'A broken part of a larger granodiorite stela, carved in 196 BC. It records
    a decree of the Egyptian priests honouring the young king Ptolemy V.


    The
    same text is written three times: in hieroglyphs (top), in Demotic (middle) and
    in ancient Greek (bottom).


    Found in 1799 at Rashid (Rosetta), it has been
    in the British Museum since 1802.'
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
