  m_text: "Because the Greek text could still be read, scholars compared it with
    the two Egyptian scripts.\n\nThomas Young recognised that the oval cartouches
    contained royal names such as Ptolemy.\n\nIn 1822 Jean-Fran\xE7ois Champollion
    showed that hieroglyphs also record sounds, and began to read them."
